(footprint "TerminalBlock_KF350_4P" (version 20221018) (generator make_lib)
  (layer "F.Cu") (descr "KF350 3.5mm 4P screw terminal (C42400616) - the v1.3 MERGED isolated contactor block. BODY geometry is the fab-proven TerminalBlock_KF350_2P extended pole-for-pole (KF350 is modular at 3.5mm/pole, so body width = 4 x 3.5 = 14.0mm; same 1.20mm drill, same body depth, same 0.30mm courtyard margin). PAD DIAMETER IS 2.20, NOT the 2P s 2.60 - annular ring 0.50mm against a JLC THT minimum of 0.15mm. MEASURED reason, not preference: with 2.60 pads the east connector column solves with 0.05mm of margin on every constraint at once (H4 courtyard, two inter-connector courtyard gaps, the ISO_CONTACTOR 2.0mm moat to J_DOOR s GND shell tab, and copper-to-edge); 2.20 buys 0.40mm along the poles and 0.40mm across them and the same solve lands at 0.09-0.35mm. Side benefit on a 30V isolated block: pole-to-pole copper gap rises 0.90 -> 1.30mm.") (attr through_hole)
